current_state:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the TinyRustLM developer portal.
  - TinyRustLM.com is the root-domain browser-local Rust/WASM app route.
  - Hugging Face search rows in TinyRustLM are metadata until MiniModel metadata names an admitted .slm with peer-offer proof and a catalog-listed or user-supplied consenting peer source, or the user locally converts source bytes with Rust, verifies the .slm, and imports it through the browser file picker.
  - When Hugging Face metadata includes safe `.safetensors` sibling names, TinyRustLM may show those source-file hints in rows and local conversion scripts, but it must not download, proxy, or treat them as runnable model bytes.
  - TinyRustLM's simple and advanced Hugging Face rows share action/source-note helpers so `P2P Import`, `Set Peer URL`, `Start Conversion`, disabled-P2P fallback, and source-file hints stay aligned.
  - TinyRustLM's simple Hugging Face lane defaults P2P on, shows P2P Import only for MiniModel matches with peer-offer proof plus validated catalog peer source or saved Known peer URL, shows Set Peer URL for proof-ready rows without a known source, shows Start Conversion for normal supported source rows, shows Review Conversion for large or unknown-size source rows, and shows one list-level warning when P2P is disabled.
  - TinyRustLM's simple P2P panel and Advanced source details can load `minimodel.peer_contact_card` JSON, validate its metadata-only direct-peer URL envelope and no-project-server flags, set the list-level Known peer URL, and refresh proof-ready rows to P2P Import without fetching model bytes; root-package `hf-peer-contact-card-ui` smoke proves that path against mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/`, and `hf-peer-contact-card-reject-ui` proves unsafe project-server-byte cards fail closed without peer import downloads.
  - Peer URL, peer contact card, and P2P toggle refreshes preserve accepted Hugging Face `.safetensors` source metadata, so `Start Conversion` / `Review Conversion` fallbacks remain available after a P2P Import handoff; the source `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` browser smoke now verifies the conversion-kit-to-peer-import path, local browser import of the peer-assembled `.slm`, and Rust/WASM generation end to end.
  - TinyRustLM's first-run transcript stays empty until real Rust/WASM generation output exists; fake recent chats, fake assistant messages, and unimplemented composer controls are not allowed. Enter-to-send uses the real submit path while Shift+Enter remains a newline.
  - Hugging Face result status must summarize real availability buckets: external records, P2P-ready matches, proof-ready matches needing a peer URL, metadata matches needing local `.slm`, external `.slm` listings needing local review, and models needing Rust conversion.
  - Start Conversion generates a self-contained local Rust handoff: save request JSON for audit/reuse, embed that JSON in the script so it can recreate the sidecar if missing, resolve workspaces/source files from environment variables, nearby paths, or a reviewed `.safetensors` beside the script; convert/pack source bytes into `.slm`; validate it; write a `tinyrustlm-conversion.receipt` that names the MiniModel share directory, `prepare-peer-share` commands, catalog snapshot, peer-source announcement/feed, local peer-serving, and metadata-only publication hints; call MiniModel `prepare-peer-share`, discover the generated manifest, catalog entry, and peer-piece directory, write a local `.minimodel-serve-peer-pieces.ps1` helper that re-inspects companion state with `inspect-peer-companion-state` before preferring `serve-peer-companion` when state exists and supports path-prefixed peer base URLs, then optionally use MiniModel `add-peer-source` for a direct with-peer entry; optionally write `write-peer-source-announcement`, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed`, run `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed`, write a feed-bound `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` snapshot after that feed preflight passes, run `inspect-catalog-snapshot` on feed-bound and normal snapshots, write metadata-only `write-peer-companion-state` handoff JSON, run `inspect-peer-companion-state`, write metadata-only `write-peer-contact-card` URL handoff JSON, and `converted-once-p2p-publish.README.txt` for metadata-only catalog publication; rely on `apply-peer-source-announcements` for maintainer drift-checked merges or `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` for batch publication; then call MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot` when publishing already-merged entries to create loadable metadata-only `models.v0.json` for reuse.
  - Source packer public CLI coverage now includes `huggingface_conversion_cli`, proving the real `tinyrustlm-slm-pack` binary writes deterministic single-file and sharded Hugging Face-shaped `.safetensors` fixtures, runs `convert-huggingface-request` against both a file path and shard directory, validates the produced `.slm`, records source-file-count preflight/receipt evidence, rejects source SHA-256 drift before writing `.slm` or receipt output, and rejects unsafe Hugging Face model ids, unsafe `.safetensors` file names, or unsafe known peer URLs before source inspection or output-directory creation.
  - Source `hf-search-ui` browser smoke now captures both Hugging Face conversion-kit branches: the normal single-file `Start Conversion` request/script/README and the large two-shard `Review Conversion` request/script/README with `source_input_mode=safetensors-shard-directory`, reviewed-directory guidance, PowerShell shard resolution, and no Hugging Face `/resolve/` byte fetch.
  - Source `hf-conversion-kit-exec` browser smoke now executes both generated conversion-kit branches: the normal single-file `Start Conversion` script and the sharded large-source `Review Conversion` script with reviewed deterministic local shard hash/byte evidence, proving Rust conversion, `source_file_count=2` receipt evidence, MiniModel share metadata, peer-source feed/catalog/companion-state inspection, contact card, and no project-server model bytes.
  - Source `hf-conversion-kit-exec` browser smoke now also executes the exact generated `Review Conversion` script against an unreconciled shard-contract mismatch, proving Rust preflight records `source_contract_status=fail` and `conversion_decision=source-contract-rejected-before-conversion`, then leaves no `.slm`, receipt, or MiniModel peer-share output.
  - Runtime native eval CLI coverage now includes `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-runtime`, which builds the documented `tinyrustlm-eval` binary and runs it against checked-in `.slm`, manifest, and eval-case fixtures before verifying the generated eval sidecar.
  - The `hf-conversion-kit-exec` browser smoke executes the exact generated Start Conversion kit plus the sharded Review Conversion kit and validates that the produced peer-source announcement feeds print MiniModel feed validation PASS output, catalog snapshots print MiniModel catalog validation PASS output, peer-companion state inspection prints PASS output, and peer contact card JSON exists, keeps the consenting peer URL, stays metadata-only, and carries no project-server model-byte proxy claim.
  - TinyRustLM exposes the generated snapshot route as `Local models.v0.json` / `Load Local Catalog`; once loaded, Hugging Face search uses that local metadata before the default MiniModel catalog, and matching rows with peer sources become `P2P Import`.
  - TinyRustLM may follow same-origin, SHA-256-bound peer-source announcement feed routes declared by a loaded catalog; those feeds are metadata only, must validate the catalog-feed envelope/no-project-server flags/duplicate model-peer rules/peer-offer route and chunk proof identity, fail closed on peer availability if verification fails, and never fetch project-hosted model bytes. MiniModel `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed` provides the matching local Rust preflight for existing feed files.
  - Empty MiniModel peer-source announcement feeds with valid metadata-only envelopes are valid availability checks and must not promote proof-ready rows to P2P Import; rows stay at Set Peer URL until a real consenting peer source is published.
  - Proof-ready MiniModel rows use metadata-only catalog entries with peer_hint_status=peer-offer-ready-known-peer-needed, peer_import_status=request-script-ready, and optional peer_source_count/peer_sources metadata; P2P import rejects canonical project/Hugging Face hosts, `www` aliases, subdomains, and trailing DNS-root-dot variants as peer sources and uses self-locating local Rust `check-peer-status`, `preflight-peer-import-request`, and `import-peer-request` receiver execution for peer-status validation, companion-state-aware fetch, assembly, verification, and import receipts with direct peer transport, piece-set SHA-256, companion-state status, fetched peer-piece bytes, assembled-from-peer-pieces status, and no-project-server-byte flags before local browser import and generation.
  - Generated P2P import scripts now run MiniModel `inspect-peer-import-request` before `check-peer-status`, giving a no-network request/manifest validation gate before peer-status, preflight, saved-preflight inspection, import, and receipt verification. They also run MiniModel `inspect-import-receipt` and `inspect-peer-import-receipt` after import, giving receipt/artifact plus receipt/request/preflight/timestamp-order validation gates before local browser import; the browser can select exactly one `.slm` plus at most one `.minimodel-receipt` sidecar, records `minimodel-p2p-import-receipt` provenance after validating strict UTC receipt timestamp, model/gate fields, peer path hints, companion-state URL/status, chunk mode, final receiver-validation contract gates, companion metadata flag, transfer evidence, and no-project-server-byte flags, renders those receipt hash/receiver-validation/route/peer/companion/artifact details in the Provenance panel after Rust/WASM acceptance, rejects receipt tampering in artifact SHA-256, companion metadata, receiver-validation gates, or timestamp fields, and rejects duplicate `.slm` or duplicate receipt selections through `local-import-ambiguous-selection`.
  - Known peer URLs must be direct `http://` peer URLs with plain DNS/IPv4 host text and safe absolute paths; query strings, fragments, traversal paths, whitespace/control paths, non-plain host text, canonical project/Hugging Face hosts, `www` aliases, subdomains, and trailing DNS-root-dot variants fail before TinyRustLM saves the URL or writes generated handoff scripts. `peer-url-unsafe-ui` proves source and mapped public-host behavior.
  - TinyRustLM can prepare local MiniModel share metadata after verified .slm import; Save Share Metadata stays metadata-only, while Save P2P Share Kit now downloads a separate share-kit-ready bundle with `peer_transfer_implementation=generated-local-minimodel-share-kit-v0`, direct MiniModel peer protocol hints, and `network_transfer_available=false` until the user runs local scripts with a consenting peer URL, plus both share and serve helper scripts. MiniModel `inspect-share-metadata` validates both bundle shapes, project-server-byte flags, chunk-list SHA-256, Merkle root, and the no-live-transfer boundary, and `share-metadata-ui` now runs that Rust validator against the actual browser downloads. Source and mapped public-root `share-metadata-import-ui` now prove local share metadata reimports as checksum-bound `Use Metadata` rows until generated catalog/manifest metadata exists, including chunk-list drift rejection, wrong local `.slm` rejection, matching local `.slm` generation, and no remote model/catalog requests. MiniModel can export/serve/fetch/reassemble known-peer pieces while broader peer discovery/relay remains later.
  - Generated share kits honor `MINIMODEL_KNOWN_PEER_BASE_URL` for reviewed local automation, and source plus mapped public-root browser-smoke mode `share-metadata-kit-exec` executes the exact downloaded `.minimodel-share-kit.ps1`, verifies generated MiniModel metadata plus feed-inspector PASS output plus catalog-inspector PASS output plus peer-companion inspection PASS output plus contact-card outputs, verifies the printed serve hint and serve helper both inspect companion state, starts local companion serving, and runs `check-peer-status` without fetching peer-piece or artifact bytes.
  - The local `Peer-source announcement/feed JSON` picker accepts full `peer-source-announcements.v0.json` feed envelopes as well as single announcements; source and mapped public-root `hf-peer-announcement-ui` smoke coverage proves a matching peer source is applied before `P2P Import`, and MiniModel `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed` covers the matching Rust preflight for existing feeds.
  - The 2026-07-03 desktop/P2P intake supports a later optional MiniModel Peer Companion only. It may help advanced users manage local identity, local piece stores, consent prompts, cache quotas, serve/fetch controls, receipts, and TinyRustLM handoff, but it remains user-run local software and does not change the browser-first or no-server-model-byte boundaries.
  - The former standalone runtime documentation corpus was preserved under docs/runtime-portal/ with a checksum manifest while its separate documentation authority is retired.
  - SLMComposer.com is no longer the canonical public app identity.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - TinyRustLM.com live public smoke uses real DNS for https://TinyRustLM.com/, reaches wasmState=loaded, stays at choose a local .slm file, and makes no /models/, Hugging Face, or MiniModel catalog requests before user action.
  - TinyRustLM.com root-package local public-host smoke maps `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/` to loopback for tests, treats the mapped origin as secure, proves `catalog-local-import` can import a real local fixture `.slm`, verify SHA-256/provenance, and run Rust/WASM generation without project-served model bytes, proves `local-import-ambiguous-selection` rejects duplicate `.slm` or duplicate receipt selections before local model selection, and proves `peer-url-unsafe-ui` rejects unsafe Known peer URLs including project/Hugging Face root-dot and subdomain host variants before request/script generation.
  - TinyRustLM.com root-package public-host share-kit smoke runs `share-metadata-kit-exec` against mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/` and proves the packaged root can save and execute the exact local P2P share kit, inspect peer-companion state, re-inspect it in the serve helper, start local MiniModel companion serving only after both the printed serve hint and helper inspect companion state, and validate peer-status metadata without fetching peer-piece or artifact bytes.
  - TinyRustLM.com root-package public-host share-metadata receiver smoke runs `share-metadata-import-ui` against mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/` and proves the packaged root rejects chunk-list drift and wrong local `.slm` artifacts, keeps valid local share metadata at `Use Metadata`, loads/generates from the matching local `.slm`, and makes only app/runtime network requests.
  - TinyRustLM.com root-package public-host P2P smoke runs `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` against mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/` and proves the packaged root completes browser conversion-kit generation, metadata-only catalog/feed publication, consenting path-prefixed MiniModel peer serving at `http://127.0.0.1:8123/peer-pieces/`, P2P handoff, manifest metadata download, `check-peer-status`, companion-aware preflight, verified peer-piece import, receipt SHA-256 matching, local browser import of the peer-assembled `.slm`, and Rust/WASM generation without project-hosted model bytes; `hf-p2p-import-receipt-reject` proves tampered receipt artifact SHA-256, companion metadata, receiver-validation gate, and timestamp sidecars are rejected before local model selection.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
